  "body": "What happens: in release mode (heavy lane), `crates/app/tests/flute_reach.rs::a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings` reports **12** rapid-in-stock findings where the test expects **3**. It fails the same way on bare `upstream/main` `1a4c69d06` (macOS, Apple Silicon). The review of PR #3770 found it (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3770#issuecomment-7121092155), and that PR does not touch the area.\n\nNot yet known: whether Linux (the cut runner) shows the same, and which merge changed the count. Candidates: #3496 (rotary seam rings), and #3777 (merged later as `cd0222d9c`, renames rapid-contact findings and edits this test file). Start with a bisect over `v0.26.0..main` in release.\n\nSeverity: a jump from 3 to 12 rapid findings is either new false positives or newly detected rapids into stock. Until that is known, read it as P2 (a red gate on main). If the extra findings are real rapids into stock that the post would accept, it is P1.\n\nDone means: the cause is named; the count is right again, or the test's expectation is changed with a decision record that explains the new number; the test is green in release on macOS and Linux.\n\nAlso seen in the same run, already tracked: `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` is outside its allowed range on macOS (#2371, macOS numbers never measured).\n",
